Use case: stylized-concept. Production asset: original fan-made 2D side-scrolling tactical stealth game sprite atlas, faithful to Metal Gear character visual references, NOT a poster.
Exact layout: landscape 1536x1152 canvas, thin cyan visible uniform grid of 8 COLUMNS by 6 ROWS, exactly 48 separated full-body sprites. Every cell 192x192. Plain solid pure magenta #FF00FF background with thin cyan grid cell borders for slicing, no checkerboard, no ground, no cast shadow, no text, no labels, no watermark. PRIORITY exact regular 8x6 table with one pose in EVERY cell. Never combine cells. EXACTLY 8 poses per row,48 in total. Every figure smaller than its cell. Each cell feet baseline 90% height, body center at50%, same scale, 18% safe margin, whole weapon/limbs fit. All sprites face RIGHT in strict side-view, readable pixel-art with crisp hand-pixelled edges, realistic adult proportions, rich shading at sprite scale.
ROW 1 and ROW 2 are actor A. ROW 3 and ROW 4 are actor B. ROW 5 and ROW 6 are actor C. Keep each character's identity, costume, silhouette, equipment and colors identical across their sixteen poses, no variation of gear.
ACTION MAP to obey precisely: {ACTIONS}
Characters: {CHARACTERS}
Render actual distinct animation poses, limbs anatomically change position along cycles, no duplicated static sprites, no motion blur. No cropped feet or firearms. No extra people. Highest fidelity to the correct game era.
